          "verdict": "malicious",
          "analysis": "The sample is a malicious backdoor that establishes persistence by creating both an init script (`/etc/init.d/%s`) and a cron job (`/etc/cron.hourly/gcc.sh`). The cron job is configured to run every 3 minutes by modifying `/etc/crontab`. The malware performs extensive system reconnaissance by reading from `/proc` to gather CPU, memory, and network information. It exfiltrates this data and receives commands via HTTP GET/POST requests. It also contains anti-forensic features, such as setting `MYSQL_HISTFILE=/dev/null` to prevent MySQL command history logging, and ensures network connectivity by executing `ifconfig $i up` on all network interfaces.",
